    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the **Austin Waves** is anchored by a high-ceiling performance expectation from **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 score makes him the undisputed focal point of the offense. Facing Aaron Civale, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a strong batting order placement, solidifying his role as our primary catalyst. **Kyle Tucker** (75.90) and **Jackson Merrill** (74.04) also serve as elite contributors; despite the matchup against Spencer Strider, **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s raw talent remains unavoidable, while **Jackson Merrill** draws a favorable spot against Dustin May, leveraging his elite speed potential despite a minor drag on his score due to May\u2019s efficiency in holding runners. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.10) rounds out the top tier, taking advantage of a high-value matchup against Jack Kochanowicz to maximize run production potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nolan Schanuel** (53.01), who hovered just outside the starting threshold. While his park factors and batting order were encouraging, his raw projection fell short of the higher-upside profiles of **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks**, who were favored for their superior matchup efficiency. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (60.70) remains a lock due to his impressive xwOBA, providing a stable floor in a challenging tilt against Luis Castillo. We are continuing to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Dominic Smith**, all of whom remain out of the immediate rotation as we navigate these game caps.\n\nOwners should maintain high alert regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, as these efficiency scores are contingent upon projected batting order placement; any downward shift in the order for **Drake Baldwin** or **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** could necessitate a re-evaluation of their daily value. Furthermore, while the wind conditions currently provide a slight boost to **Coby Mayo** and **Jacob Wilson**, keep an eye on shifting forecasts in their respective stadiums. With **Josh Lowe** (60.92) rounding out the outfield, we are prioritizing high-contact, high-speed profiles to maximize our 5x5 output against this slate of right-handed starters.",
